{"assets":["/statement-assets/ffcabd6f45e30983aa5ebd3072d501772b84597a4efd547ce0588b0c8f369cd1.png","/statement-assets/524f6cefe80f6391f23c7095972d39a63beda1585c8b8331c896976e4071ae07.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1065","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Up and Down the Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_(graph_theory)"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tree"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" with $$$n$$$ vertices; its root is vertex $$$1$$$. Also there is a token, initially placed in the root. You can move the token to other vertices. Let's assume current vertex of token is $$$v$$$, then you make any of the following two possible moves: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" move down to any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"leaf"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in subtree of $$$v$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if vertex $$$v$$$ is a leaf, then move up to the parent no more than $$$k$$$ times. In other words, if $$$h(v)$$$ is the depth of vertex $$$v$$$ (the depth of the root is $$$0$$$), then you can move to vertex $$$to$$$ such that $$$to$$$ is an ancestor of $$$v$$$ and $$$h(v) - k \\le h(to)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider that root is not a leaf (even if its degree is $$$1$$$). Calculate the maximum number of different leaves you can visit during one sequence of moves."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\lt n \\le 10^6$$$) — the number of vertices in the tree and the restriction on moving up, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n - 1$$$ integers $$$p_2, p_3, \\dots, p_n$$$, where $$$p_i$$$ is the parent of vertex $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the input represents a valid tree, rooted at $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the maximum possible number of different leaves you can visit."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 1\n1 1 3 3 4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 2\n1 1 2 3 4 5 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The graph from the first example: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ffcabd6f45e30983aa5ebd3072d501772b84597a4efd547ce0588b0c8f369cd1.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of the optimal ways is the next one: $$$1 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 1 \\rightarrow 5 \\rightarrow 3 \\rightarrow 7 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The graph from the second example: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/524f6cefe80f6391f23c7095972d39a63beda1585c8b8331c896976e4071ae07.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of the optimal ways is the next one: $$$1 \\rightarrow 7 \\rightarrow 5 \\rightarrow 8$$$. Note that there is no way to move from $$$6$$$ to $$$7$$$ or $$$8$$$ and vice versa."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1065F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1065/problem/F"}